WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:01.020
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.150
- Let's round out the
hour with one last story

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.010
that I hope brings a smile to your face.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.232
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.232 --> 00:00:07.381
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.381 --> 00:00:09.270
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.310
So you all might know
that I'm an avid reader.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.360
My mama helped me develop

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.520
a love for reading at a very early age,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.580
and that instilled a
passion I have to this day,

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.400
but too many kids don't
have access to any books.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.390
That's why I'm obsessed

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.620
with the West Virginia teen,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.630
who's made it her mission to get books

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.460
to every single preschool child

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.440
in her state living in poverty,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.273
so cool.

00:00:29.273 --> 00:00:30.630
She's just getting started, y'all.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.490
Let's say hi to Rania.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.461
What inspired this?

00:00:33.461 --> 00:00:34.369
(audience cheering)

00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:36.000
(Kelly clapping)

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.370
- I have always been a bibliophile,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.590
like you, my entire life.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.640
So in middle school, I
had a classics book club,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.670
but in ninth grade, I
was working on a project

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.470
to set up a small library

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.150
for young migrant girls

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.640
when I learned about the vast book deserts

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.250
that exist in our own country.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.010
I learned about them
before in other countries,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.200
because both of my grandfathers

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.700
grew up in book deserts,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.630
and they were able

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.670
to escape poverty through literacy,

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.503
so I like to say

00:01:06.503 --> 00:01:10.080
that literacy is truly
the ladder out of poverty.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.160
- Yeah.
- And so I combine

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.920
my classics book club with my passion

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.050
for ending the book desert

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.210
to the LiTEArary Society,

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.660
and we are a 501(c)(3)
nonprofit organization

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.030
with the mission of ending book deserts

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.580
for disadvantaged preschool children,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.280
and in this country,
that means Head Start,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.920
and so far, I've donated brand-new books

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.160
to over 16,000 children in Head Start

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.960
in all 50 states,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.160
and these are

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.190
all new, amazing, beloved Pre-K titles

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.420
that we donate.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.080
- Oh my gosh, you are amazing.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.060
(audience clapping)

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.800
So are there any plans,

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.780
like big plans for expansion?

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.613
- Oh yes,

00:01:49.613 --> 00:01:52.410
we have a lot coming up and in progress.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.300
I'm currently on a road tour,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.280
and surprising Head Start centers

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.750
with brand-new books

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.640
for each child in these centers,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.330
and I'm also working on
a US Senate resolution,

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.430
called One Book at a Time Day

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.890
to bring awareness to book deserts,

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.690
and how we, as individuals,

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.240
can all make a big impact,

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.220
and I also wrote and illustrated

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.890
a series of children's picture books

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.920
about Billy Bob, who is
an Appalachian bunny.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:20.850
I don't know if you can see him.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.440
He's right there.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.600
- And it is sold in stores,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.790
at Barnes &amp; Noble and on Amazon,

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.500
and all of the profits

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.230
are going to my One Book
at a Time initiative

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.820
to get more brand-new books

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.620
to children in Head Start.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.617
- That's incredible.

00:02:35.617 --> 00:02:37.140
(audience clapping)

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.080
You are such a great
example of a young woman,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.760
such a great heart, so intelligent,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.500
and by the way, you are...

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.990
It's mesmerizing how beautiful you are.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.780
Your smile, your eyes, you just light up.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.980
I just needed to tell you that too,

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.050
but it's just you're such a great example

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.720
for all these young kids and for adults.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.090
You can make such a big
impact on your community,

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.620
and people don't even realize how,

00:02:58.620 --> 00:02:59.760
and you figured out how,

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:00.750
and this is really important.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.658
I'm liking your post
right now, Rania, okay?

00:03:02.658 --> 00:03:03.491
(audience clapping)

00:03:03.491 --> 00:03:04.324
- Oh, thank you so much.

00:03:04.324 --> 00:03:05.280
(heart dinging)

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.780
- Absolutely.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.700
Well, that's not all.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.780
Our season-long partner,

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.190
Pilot Pen, makers of Frixion,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.210
the go-to erasable pen

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.290
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.160
want to celebrate

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.920
those creating opportunities and ladders,

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:17.820
like you were saying,

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:18.810
and they want to do this

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:19.830
for people just like you,

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:20.970
just having such a big heart,

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.560
so they're going to give you $1,000.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.442
How's that sound?

00:03:23.442 --> 00:03:25.338
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.421
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:28.980
Oh, thank you so...

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:29.813
I can't wait

00:03:29.813 --> 00:03:32.070
to surprise the children in Headstart.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.260
Thank you so, so much.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.310
- Absolutely.
- [Rania] I-

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.690
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.550
Thank you so much for taking the time,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.383
and thank you so much

00:03:39.383 --> 00:03:41.700
for doing what you do for so many,

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.470
and thank you to all our guests this hour:

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.270
Marlee Matlin, Tyler Posey,

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:48.720
Maggie, Andrew, Connie, T, Jeremy Rosado,

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.150
Kyle Selzer, Michelle McConkey,

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:54.000
and all our friends and partners at WRAL.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.020
Y'all have a great day,

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.943
and if it's not, try and change it.

